#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119577 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1d809050-9477-5de6-8c95-7294804e7b69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4943" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \t\\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-2t,-4-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ -7(5+4t)+5(3-2t)+(-4-3t) & =-65 \\\\ -35-28t+15-10t-4-3t & =-65 \\\\ -41t & =-41 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5+4(1),3-2(1),-4-3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,1,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9 , 1, -7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119578 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/id #uuid "c1576b30-9142-5884-b654-7ade7a765ec7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4944" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad  \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle .\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z-7 & =0 \\\\ 4x-3y+2z & =7 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,3+t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ 4(1+2t)-3(3+t)+2\\cdot 1 & =7 \\\\ 4+8t-9-3t+2 & =7 \\\\ 5t & =10 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),3+(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5 , 5, 1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119579 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/id #uuid "f952e670-a673-5c15-913b-c396e8885142" :question/math-academy-id "e-4945" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/assets/2a24a49f0fc47c235776597df655e75be9c68cffbb7988db16b36d9200f801bc.png)" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4y+6z+25 & =0 \\\\ 3(3-4t)+4(-1+2t)+6(2+3t)+25 & =0 \\\\ 9-12t-4+8t+12+18t+25 & =0 \\\\ 14t & =-42 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4(-3)=15 \\\\ y=-1+2(-3)=-7 \\\\ z=2+3(-3)=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ff1b670-d9ce-578f-abed-beb705375599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338725} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f5a6ad-f90e-57b3-9d8a-f1d55a9c1f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-5,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338726} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6729de-aff7-5c4c-98ad-1bb06eb79a23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338727} {:answer/id #uuid "eac8ebca-c530-5195-acb2-b6292ade13da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338728} {:answer/id #uuid "4f6b7658-2157-5f1b-b131-5b91d1e140f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-8,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d6729de-aff7-5c4c-98ad-1bb06eb79a23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338727} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f06fdb5-06f0-5457-8b29-4b3079bc722a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d28c265-18d6-5656-afcf-7f8222829274" :question/math-academy-id "q-108311" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,-2,3⟩+t⟨0,3,-1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩=-7.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ ⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ 5+3(-2+3t)+(-2)(3-t) & =-7 \\\\ 5-6+9t-6+2t & =-7 \\\\ 11t & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=0$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5,-2+3(0),3-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,-2,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad1f5c5e-9bfc-542f-b83d-9cd12da5c2e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,4,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338732} {:answer/id #uuid "031f0ab7-98e5-5ef1-b694-26f424e0c1fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338733} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0767ba-c8fe-5d02-98cb-a2daad8cd428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,2,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338734} {:answer/id #uuid "b90c5c3a-2f79-5901-856b-ccae222540c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338735} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e8c10b-4c6c-548e-8a40-af66b3fc3888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad1f5c5e-9bfc-542f-b83d-9cd12da5c2e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,4,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338732} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bd20147-884b-5aad-8617-b8c00cdeb58e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aae7d446-6165-5274-a5d2-5622980a25ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-108313" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-1⟩+t⟨5,-2,4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩=22.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ 0(3+5t)+1(-2t)+(-2)(-1+4t) & =22 \\\\ -2t+2-8t & =22 \\\\ -10t & =20 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-2),-2(-2),-1+4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,4,-9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-7,4,-9).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39aba5e9-0c9f-540f-b74d-16c2a40e488a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338739} {:answer/id #uuid "4a8b0c89-d047-564c-bd0f-7be376601439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338740} {:answer/id #uuid "cfb87311-ed0d-5027-8c5f-f54464f4e605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338741} {:answer/id #uuid "354ae279-9213-5947-a40b-84a3fdcefc17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338742} {:answer/id #uuid "ff97cc03-27a1-58d6-8889-d7dde92b0edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "354ae279-9213-5947-a40b-84a3fdcefc17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338742} :answer-field/id #uuid "39c5cc2a-6c44-5296-ba70-0e923a5a0298" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b4368ee-9c42-51ca-8e68-cd3ecf43a30f" :question/math-academy-id "q-108323" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:x-3y+2z=12.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y+2z & =12 \\\\ 1(7+2t)-3(3+t)+2(1-t) & =12 \\\\ 7+2t-9-3t+2-2t & =12 \\\\ -3t & =12 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2(-4)=-1 \\\\ y=3+(-4)=-1 \\\\ z=1-(-4)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-1,-1,5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d50a837-ca84-5b35-afa7-a0e80577837c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338746} {:answer/id #uuid "40f90ea6-b8bd-5440-95fd-4906a3f4258e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338747} {:answer/id #uuid "625cd6b8-23e5-5238-a742-0f86a50b9c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338748} {:answer/id #uuid "8bfad242-416e-5d84-9cfd-dc9b87a22ae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338749} {:answer/id #uuid "2b42cfe2-b6cb-5d52-b4ed-b078e822c042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,6,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d50a837-ca84-5b35-afa7-a0e80577837c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338746} :answer-field/id #uuid "c46ebfc7-3818-597b-9fff-12142b7425c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338745}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60f0cd70-b4b4-5b35-85ba-563cceee9aad" :question/math-academy-id "q-108326" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=6+2t \\\\ y=5+t \\\\ z=-3-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x+3y-4z=-43.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+3y-4z & =-43 \\\\ 5(6+2t)+3(5+t)-4(-3-3t) & =-43 \\\\ 30+10t+15+3t+12+12t & =-43 \\\\ 25t & =-100 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=6+2(-4) \\\\ y=5+(-4) \\\\ z=-3-3(-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-2,1,9).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0685c34e-7f8c-542c-a8df-082d2bd2d0dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338753} {:answer/id #uuid "0ebcf735-1d00-575e-9786-8bd7db6f13d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,13,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338754} {:answer/id #uuid "9c7549da-aa05-5f9a-b970-554a5ae24af8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338755} {:answer/id #uuid "55bad4ad-1cc1-5384-974a-a376f90f80bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,9,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338756} {:answer/id #uuid "4847ee0f-9e5c-5369-bbda-8d74f3fffe1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,-1,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0685c34e-7f8c-542c-a8df-082d2bd2d0dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338753} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aabbaa0-da27-5e13-92cc-3d64261bc76d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36683b19-26fd-5526-a537-6298e5ac4183" :question/math-academy-id "q-108337" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3t \\\\ y=5+2t \\\\ z=-7+t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+3y+5z-11=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+5z-11 & =0 \\\\ 4(9-3t)+3(5+2t)+5(-7+t) & =11 \\\\ 36-12t+15+6t-35+5t & =11 \\\\ -t & =-5 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3(5)=-6 \\\\ y=5+2(5)=15 \\\\ z=-7+5=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-6,15,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338758 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "901d1af5-10b0-5cfe-8738-ed43d3b4f75d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338760} {:answer/id #uuid "ba3d75a8-d756-5a68-b38b-92b969430fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338761} {:answer/id #uuid "2abef77e-dcdc-501b-bd8e-68b7273aee3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-5,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338762} {:answer/id #uuid "0c958dd1-085a-5ae3-b8e0-7faec2e6a810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338763} {:answer/id #uuid "d0d71fc4-41cf-5be8-b326-95b9f8e7974f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,0,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba3d75a8-d756-5a68-b38b-92b969430fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338761} :answer-field/id #uuid "41a4b91a-936a-5a70-b800-e3f1b5e58981" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "095e7ba7-485c-5158-9e30-e0ada8d73941" :question/math-academy-id "q-33194" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,1,0⟩+t⟨1,3,2⟩,\\,Π:3x-2y+4z+6=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z+6 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+4z & =-6 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ ⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ 3(2+t)-2(1+3t)+4(2t) & =-6 \\\\ 6+3t-2-6t+8t & =-6 \\\\ 5t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+(-2),1+3(-2),2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(0,-5,-4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338765 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8747eb3a-fc54-5776-8718-88e3f3f86e1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,4,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338767} {:answer/id #uuid "da77f2aa-64b5-5ca1-ac36-02ec2be0ec2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,8,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338768} {:answer/id #uuid "bbdaedf4-03bc-5e84-8bce-25632aeb6b11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338769} {:answer/id #uuid "317ddedd-6ce1-50d7-ac8a-6702106d586e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,2,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338770} {:answer/id #uuid "fa623a79-e505-5608-88cf-de0b2ecb19f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,8,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da77f2aa-64b5-5ca1-ac36-02ec2be0ec2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,8,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338768} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdd9ea5c-674e-5100-b381-fa89099eac19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338766}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2bb1b52f-f5e4-5ec9-a0da-60cc3db1db86" :question/math-academy-id "q-33201" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-4⟩+t⟨2,4,3⟩,\\,Π:4x+3y+4z-60=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+4z-60 & =0 \\\\ 4x+3y+4z & =60 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ ⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ 4(3+2t)+3(4t)+4(-4+3t) & =60 \\\\ 12+8t+12t-16+12t & =60 \\\\ 32t & =64 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+2(2),4(2),-4+3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,8,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,8,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a69b22d8-5f30-5e05-81bb-243ed724e1d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-4, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117553} {:answer/id #uuid "cdce1910-9bcc-5251-b118-6aa04aaeb35a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117554} {:answer/id #uuid "06faf094-268f-5487-9e0a-8dda830b16c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8, 1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117555} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea6e821-2c68-5890-9921-7e7988992607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-4, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117556} {:answer/id #uuid "79a2209b-6180-5a7d-9efd-5b7a99c8eed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7, 1,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ea6e821-2c68-5890-9921-7e7988992607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-4, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117556} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe66adf4-1b34-5a67-af27-8e9f1215ce5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117552}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49e4fa98-401d-5c2d-a49c-1997a8550033" :question/math-academy-id "q-33203" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-5,0,1⟩+t⟨-3,1,0⟩,\\,Π:-3x+y-2z+27=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+y-2z+27 & =0 \\\\ -3x+y-2z & =-27 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ ⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ -3(-5-3t)+1\\cdot t-2\\cdot 1 & =-27 \\\\ 15+9t+t-2 & =-27 \\\\ 10t & =-40 \\\\ t & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-4$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-5-3(-4),-4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,-4,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,-4,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338772 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42436bde-7a95-5fd0-8e7e-17a262ce6c77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,8,14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338774} {:answer/id #uuid "42d6c4ce-4668-5bee-bc85-f8090d692fc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-2,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338775} {:answer/id #uuid "bbfef096-0506-51a2-91cc-3d099bc1c06d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338776} {:answer/id #uuid "0a291b95-adc1-50e4-a3c9-74dbc1d576c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,4,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338777} {:answer/id #uuid "7391d614-f965-5593-97fd-d62ce5d9eb1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(14,8,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42436bde-7a95-5fd0-8e7e-17a262ce6c77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,8,14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338774} :answer-field/id #uuid "e21fd410-8d68-5c04-9351-bb619c018421" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eaab1f60-24fb-5572-8cfb-474f418bf09f" :question/math-academy-id "q-33205" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-1,-2,6⟩+t⟨2,5,4⟩,\\,Π:x+2y+z-33=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z-33 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+z & =33 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ ⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ -1+2t+2(-2+5t)+6+4t & =33 \\\\ -1+2t-4+10t+6+4t & =33 \\\\ 16t & =32 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-1+2(2),-2+5(2),6+4(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,8,14⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(3,8,14).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80c089cc-0c53-590f-a42b-18de8a2f4284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338781} {:answer/id #uuid "cf1474a9-6277-548c-a070-2baaee6f31e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338782} {:answer/id #uuid "db9083f7-cfcf-51f1-8808-75c0cd201018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338783} {:answer/id #uuid "15fe6147-2917-5137-a867-859d28ee769a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-19,-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338784} {:answer/id #uuid "06756fbd-4f03-5156-9987-20bc62440bba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,9,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15fe6147-2917-5137-a867-859d28ee769a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-19,-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338784} :answer-field/id #uuid "4312fcfe-ca68-5a99-a8f2-1e923eca295b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5b04adfc-e5b7-5f8d-8dfe-dffbf8b2c66f" :question/math-academy-id "q-33968" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,3,2⟩+w⟨-5,-2,-1⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-12,10,6⟩+s⟨1,0,4⟩+t⟨2,6,0⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨1,0,4⟩\\times ⟨2,6,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-24i+8j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-24,8,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =⟨-12,10,6⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1,3,2⟩+w⟨-5,-2,-1⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ ⟨1-5w,3-2w,2-w⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ -24(1-5w)+8(3-2w)+6(2-w) & =404 \\\\ -24+120w+24-16w+12-6w & =404 \\\\ 98w & =392 \\\\ w & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=4$ into the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨1-5(4),3-2(4),2-(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-19,-5,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(-19,-5,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f133d3b6-1df8-5d6c-a6e1-4cc7271626f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,-20,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338788} {:answer/id #uuid "be2cec85-34f3-5890-b64d-cb09a4374ed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,13,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338789} {:answer/id #uuid "c69d3d30-d776-59df-a2e8-50ce184ae06f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,31,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338790} {:answer/id #uuid "b5508fe3-d17e-5b82-bd8a-e33fc74d4104" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338791} {:answer/id #uuid "0de8c113-3190-5840-8fb9-f5c7bb12f629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,13,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be2cec85-34f3-5890-b64d-cb09a4374ed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,13,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338789} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3f89eb7-32ce-58ab-af26-6895ea450c74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e5fa2c2-85ce-5f18-afd6-dedce5453b43" :question/math-academy-id "q-33988" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-4⟩+t⟨-5,2,7⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩=30.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩ & =30 \\\\ ⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩ & =30 \\\\ 2(5-5t)+3(3+2t)-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 10-10t+9+6t-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 3t & =15 \\\\ t & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5-5(5),3+2(5),-4+7(5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-20,13,31⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-20,13,31).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338793 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbe0c409-6b66-5562-8460-88b49d1631e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-6,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338795} {:answer/id #uuid "b4cd441e-6b76-5604-b488-9f2f7b982c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-6,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338796} {:answer/id #uuid "9edd9c5d-e4d7-5d63-86af-b2962ba7f512" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338797} {:answer/id #uuid "95109580-9e46-5465-a314-e4bbaab31df2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338798} {:answer/id #uuid "d4cda5ee-fd27-50ce-91dc-b978380a5df9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,2,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9edd9c5d-e4d7-5d63-86af-b2962ba7f512" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338797} :answer-field/id #uuid "520d4b40-44ef-5cda-bca1-64895daa8f36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36894dd9-ad4f-58c5-8fd6-dfd9706bcecb" :question/math-academy-id "q-73984" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,2,7⟩+t⟨-5,-6,0⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩=-24.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩ & =-24 \\\\ ⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩ & =-24 \\\\ -6(3-5t)+5(2-6t)+4\\cdot 7 & =-24 \\\\ -18+30t+10-30t+28 & =-24 \\\\ 20 & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63533bfb-1aaf-53a5-bce6-0a04e315530b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338802} {:answer/id #uuid "a4284848-979c-5fae-989a-3cd17ed040d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338803} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea3d7cc-1f42-5183-b17e-629a43310bde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338804} {:answer/id #uuid "e49af1b9-e47a-5fee-a40d-19324bedec52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338805} {:answer/id #uuid "14aea272-0f72-538a-9340-815fdbcd24ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-3,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4284848-979c-5fae-989a-3cd17ed040d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338803} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f7137c2-9897-5ea1-92cf-de9f34c1bf13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb2bf85c-9bb4-5c89-8fe8-0cc8aac7e5a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-73987" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨5,2,-4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩=36.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ ⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ 2(1+5t)-3(1+2t)+5(1-4t) & =36 \\\\ 2+10t-3-6t+5-20t & =36 \\\\ -16t & =32 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+5(-2),1+2(-2),1-4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-9,-3,9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-9,-3,9).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2699e9b5-cdb9-5d08-af40-101189a9fe62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(19,10,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338809} {:answer/id #uuid "1b15c630-a693-5679-819b-eea883f61546" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,11,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338810} {:answer/id #uuid "5d516cd8-dadb-5457-b33b-e27837b4fcd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,-1,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338811} {:answer/id #uuid "09fde5db-22e0-5375-bf7a-30854d8d9851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,8,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338812} {:answer/id #uuid "d6385c11-cd80-5693-b906-783769c98896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b15c630-a693-5679-819b-eea883f61546" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,11,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338810} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c554705-9568-55b3-99b7-44461a69d4ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "748eb406-dbd6-5954-8c6a-51567bc19c1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73993" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=2-3t \\\\ z=-2-6t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x-2y+4z-132=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y+4z-132 & =0 \\\\ 5(3-5t)-2(2-3t)+4(-2-6t) & =132 \\\\ 15-25t-4+6t-8-24t & =132 \\\\ -43t & =129 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5(-3)=18 \\\\ y=2-3(-3)=11 \\\\ z=-2-6(-3)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(18,11,16).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df5ac142-a41e-558b-94e2-54be6e32075e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338816} {:answer/id #uuid "5cdda2c9-4fe5-5bb2-9519-342c31cd32ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,2,-8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338817} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9408c3-0eb4-5b30-8808-98420723e10f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338818} {:answer/id #uuid "105d22a0-f100-57a5-83c4-a6a5d8b76d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338819} {:answer/id #uuid "410b9713-26d7-5617-92d8-b56182622870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,21,-14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f9408c3-0eb4-5b30-8808-98420723e10f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338818} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7732099-3c9a-500e-a0a3-ab40ac1da9d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45a75007-267d-50a7-b554-5511306a0ee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-74003" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=5-t \\\\ y=4+2t \\\\ z=-6-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+6y-3z-130=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+6y-3z-130 & =0 \\\\ 4(5-t)+6(4+2t)-3(-6-3t) & =130 \\\\ 20-4t+24+12t+18+9t & =130 \\\\ 17t & =68 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-4=1 \\\\ y=4+2(4)=12 \\\\ z=-6-3(4)=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(1,12,-18).$"}]}
